<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; Cultures</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: Cultures of Egypt &amp; North Africa</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on 3 cultures of Egypt &amp; North Africa, from the Nubians to the Garamantes. Read their profiles, then answer.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/profiles?kind=culture&amp;region=Egypt%20%26%20North%20Africa">Open the cultures &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the cultures in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the cultures from 1 (the earliest to begin) to 3 (the latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Kerma culture</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Garamantes</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Nubians</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Match the cultures to their homelands</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right homeland next to each culture. Their profiles will help.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Nubians</li><li>Kerma culture</li><li>Garamantes</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>The Fezzan region of southern Libya, centred on the Wadi al-Ajjal</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Upper Nubia, in present-day northern and central Sudan, centred on Kerma</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Nubia, from southern Egypt to northern Sudan</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p><b>Nubians</b>. Its profile says: &#8220;The Nubians are indigenous to the Nile valley between southern Egypt and northern Sudan, where Neolithic settlements date back to 7000 BCE, and they speak Nilo-Saharan Nubian languages with Arabic as a second language.&#8221; Find one piece of evidence on the profile for this, and say how we know it.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p><b>Kerma culture</b>. Its profile says: &#8220;Kerma grew from a fortified village into a city of about 25 hectares, the capital of a centralised Nubian kingdom that controlled the Nile from the First to the Fourth Cataract.&#8221; Find one piece of evidence on the profile for this, and say how we know it.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p><b>Garamantes</b>. Its profile says: &#8220;The Garamantes mined fossil water from under the desert through a network of tunnels and shafts, the foggaras, which supported farming and a large population in the Fezzan.&#8221; Find one piece of evidence on the profile for this, and say how we know it.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose two of these cultures that lived at the same time. What did they have in common, and what set them apart?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/profiles?kind=culture&amp;region=Egypt%20%26%20North%20Africa. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: Cultures of Egypt &amp; North Africa</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the cultures in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Nubians <span>c. 7000 BCE to today</span></li><li>Kerma culture <span>c. 2500 BCE – c. 1500 BCE</span></li><li>Garamantes <span>c. 1000 BCE – c. 700 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Match the cultures to their homelands</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Nubians <span>3: Nubia, from southern Egypt to northern Sudan</span></li><li>Kerma culture <span>2: Upper Nubia, in present-day northern and central Sudan, centred on Kerma</span></li><li>Garamantes <span>1: The Fezzan region of southern Libya, centred on the Wadi al-Ajjal</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers use details from the profiles.</p></section></div></details>
